# TFIXU 5 / ui 9 (owner decision, 2026-10-11): the LIVE PLAY keyboard is a scale-degree keyboard in
# the song's key and scale (option a): note = 12*(3+octv) + song_key + scale_step(k), where
# scale_step walks the scale across octaves as k rises.
wait 300
newsong 0                          # Empty: C major, so the values are absolute
expect songkey 0
expect songscale 0
expect playnote0.0 36              # C2
expect playnote1.0 38
expect playnote3.0 41
expect playnote4.0 43
expect playnote7.0 48              # the next C at the octave
expect playnote0.1 48              # OCT+ transposes by an octave
# enter LIVE and play the scale on the panel keys
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 50
expect mode 1
tap SEL
expect layer 1
events live_play_scale_events.txt
tapkey w0
tapkey w1
tapkey w2
eventsstop
dump live_play_scale.json
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 60
expect mode 0
# r1 #3: the top of the range folds down by octaves instead of piling the high keys onto 127.
songkeyscale 0 0                    # C major
expect playnote26.4 117             # raw 129 -> 117 (the old code clamped to 127)
songkeyscale 11 0                   # B major
expect playnote26.4 116             # raw 140 -> 116
songkeyscale 11 3                   # B penta
expect playnote26.4 121             # raw 157 -> 121
songkeyscale 1 4                    # C# chromatic
expect playnote26.4 111             # raw 111: already in range, unchanged
# every key of every scale, folded by whole octaves and in range (throws the scale table at it)
scalecheck
